WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.460
Glad you're here. Welcome to Models &amp; Agents Episode 82. It's June 16th, 2026.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.960
Your daily briefing on the AI models and agents that are changing everything.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:14.540
And no, not those kinds of models and agents. Let's get into it.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:21.780
Export Controls on Fable 5 now block the exact code-fixing workflows defenders rely on daily.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:27.900
Simon Willison published a detailed breakdown showing how Fable 5's refusal to fix vulnerable

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:34.380
open source code triggered enforcement actions. Researchers found the model rejected a direct security

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:40.620
review prompt, but accepted a multi-step fix this code request. That output then became working

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:46.480
test scripts for defensive patching. The capability sits at the center of the find fixed test loop

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:52.620
security teams run every day. Regulators appear to have treated defensive bug fixing as a prohibited

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.440
cyber capability. The result limits access to models that could improve patching inside the

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:04.520
United States. Watch for further clarification on whether routine code review prompts stay restricted.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:11.280
This development lands in the ongoing conversation around safety and policy that we have tracked since

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:17.480
Episode 81. It raises fresh questions about how export rules will separate attack generation from

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:25.460
everyday defensive tooling. Nemotron 3 Ultra arrived as a 550 billion total parameter mixture of

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:32.660
experts model with 55 billion active parameters. The hybrid Mamba attention design was pre-trained on

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:39.160
20 trillion tokens and then extended to a 1 million token context window. Post-training combined

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:44.360
supervised fine-tuning, reinforcement learning, and multi-teacher on policy distillation.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:50.620
The model reportedly delivers up to six times higher inference throughput than current public frontier

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:57.420
models while matching accuracy. In video open source the base post-trained and quantized checkpoints

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:03.180
plus the training data on hugging face. This release continues the open weight models arc we covered

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:09.520
yesterday and narrows the performance gap with closed frontier systems. Builders working on long

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:15.360
running autonomous agents should test the 1 million context checkpoints for workflow memory tasks.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:23.020
The Ling and Ring 2.6 family upgrades the Ling 2.0 base through architectural migration pre-training

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:29.780
and large-scale post-training. Ling 2.6 targets instant response with high capability per token.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:38.440
Ring 2.6 targets deeper reasoning and advanced agent workflows. A hybrid linear attention design

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:44.400
combines lightning attention with MLA to improve long-context training and decoding efficiency.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:50.640
Additional techniques include evolutionary chain of thought, linguistic unit policy optimization,

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:57.220
and the K-POP RL framework. All checkpoints are open sourced. Teams building low-latency

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:02.140
agentic systems should benchmark Ling 2.6 against current production stacks.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:08.020
Adam Mame is a two-stage training recipe that aligns reasoning language to the query

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:14.480
language without accuracy trade-offs. Stage 1 fine tunes on naturally occurring reasoning traces

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:21.640
across five languages. Stage 2 uses a modified group relative policy optimization where a query

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:27.920
conditioned alignment factor grows during training. The method improves language fidelity and token

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:34.580
efficiency on 12 languages across two benchmarks while preserving accuracy. Largest gains appear on

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:41.720
resource languages. Multi-lingual agent developers should experiment with the GRPO adaptation on their

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:49.220
current fine tunes. Quick talk is a C++ BPE tokenizer that produces bite identical output to

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:56.600
TikTokin. It runs 4 to 11 times faster than the Python version and 2 to 3.6 times faster than

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:07.240
BPE Open AI on Apple M1 Silicon. The project supports clone 100,000, 0200,000, GPT OSS, Lama 3, and

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:13.800
Quen 2. Five-thirds tokenizers, it ships with a hand-compiled pre-tokenizer plus dense caches

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:19.960
for merged checks. Any pipeline doing heavy tokenization should swap in quick talk for immediate

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:26.360
throughput gains. Hermy's agent now lets the delegate tool spawn background sub-agents via the

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:32.920
new async delegation tool set. Sub-agents run independently so the parent chat can continue while

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:40.640
tasks execute. Users can later steer, check status, or collect results. The update introduces explicit

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:47.100
sub-agent isolation and synchronous versus asynchronous trade-offs. This change moves the agents and

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:53.120
tool use conversation forward from yesterday's coverage by addressing reliability of long horizon

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:59.620
workflows. Developers using Hermes should test the async path on multi-step tasks that previously

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:05.900
stalled the main session. Adams lets users describe an app in plain language and then deploys AI

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:12.980
agents to build, edit, refine, deploy, and market the application. The system targets non-developers

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:18.480
who want to ship functional products through iterative natural language direction. No specific

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:24.500
license or pricing details were released. Teams exploring no-code, agentic app generation should

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:29.060
try the public demo to assess current output quality on realistic product ideas.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:35.780
Google Cloud introduced the Open Knowledge Format, a vendor neutral markdown spec for giving AI

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:43.920
agents curated context. OKF formalizes the LLM wiki pattern as a directory of markdown files with

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:50.520
YAML Front Matter, where each concept requires only a type field. Google released reference tools,

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:56.860
a working Python consumer, and an interactive bundle explorer. The format is positioned as an

00:05:56.860 --> 00:06:02.380
alternative to retrieval augmented generation for supplying agents with structured human readable

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:09.080
context. Agent Builders needing portable version controllable knowledge should evaluate OKF bundles

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:15.300
against their current context injection methods. Phone harness provides a mixed action execution harness

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:22.380
and benchmark that lets phone agents combine GUI actions, device CLI commands, and host side tools.

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:30.540
On the annotated evaluation split, it reaches a 75% pass rate, 12.9 points above the strongest

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:36.880
non-phone harness baseline. The benchmark requires observable side effects rather than just plausible

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:43.540
final answers. Mobile agent developers should examine the harness for tasks that need verifiable real

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:50.180
world effects beyond screen taps. A tutorial now walks through setting up docking parts in a stable

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:55.340
Python environment. It covers handling colab dependency issues and generating custom

00:06:55.340 --> 00:07:01.440
multi-page PDFs with text, columns, tables, shapes, and images. The pipeline extracts words,

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:07.260
characters, and lines with page level coordinates. Render's visual overlays and exports structured

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:14.220
JSON or CSV. Anyone ingesting complex PDFs for retrieval, augmented generation, or agent memory

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:19.860
should run the pipeline on their current document corpus. OK, let's pop the hood on quick talk.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:26.000
Tokenization speed is really a memory access and data structure problem that compounds across

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:33.200
every forward pass. Quick talk keeps the exact backtracking BPE algorithm, but replaces the general

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:39.920
Ragex pre-tokenizer with a hand-compiled one. It adds a two-byte try for longest match walking,

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:46.460
plus dense caches for merge validity checks. These changes cut memory traffic enough to deliver

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:52.340
four to 11 times speedups on Apple M1, while remaining byte identical to Tiktokin.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:59.000
The quality of the resulting tokens stays unchanged. The approach works best when you control

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:05.520
the full ingestion pipeline and can afford a native dependency. If you are already bottlenecked on

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:11.120
Python tokenization loops or running high-volume batch encoding, the swap is low-risk and

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:16.900
immediately measurable. The gacha that bites most teams is forgetting to verify byte identity on

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:23.160
their specific tokenizer variant after the switch. Test Nemotron 3 Ultra 1 million context

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:27.840
checkpoints on long horizon agent workflows that previously hit context limits.

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:34.400
Swap quick talk into any heavy tokenization pipeline for immediate four times or greater throughput

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:41.220
without changing token IDs. Experiment with Hermes agent's async delegation on multi-step tasks

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:48.380
that currently stall the parent chat. Load Google Clouds OKF reference tools and compare curated

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:53.460
mark-down bundles against your existing retrieval augmented generation context strategy.

00:08:54.280 --> 00:09:00.120
Further clarification is expected on Fable 5 export control scope for defensive security prompts.

